function infoCc_injectToCodex()
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addCategory', 'cc_cat', 'Cosmic Chronicles'%_t, 'data/textures/icons/trading.png')

    -- Full Feature Breakdown
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'cc_cat', 'cc_cat_c0', 'Full Feature Breakdown'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a0', 'The Rumormonger System'%_t, 'Adds dynamic background chatter and interactive rumor-gathering to all NPC stations in the game. Features a rapidly expanding registry of over 60+ unique, localized lore strings.\n\nKey Mechanics:\n\n- Ambient Chatter: Stations run a highly optimized 35-second background chatter loop, periodically broadcasting floating overhead text based on their specific type and current situation. (Global sector cooldown is 30 seconds with a 50% speech probability).\n- Interaction: Players can dock and access a direct dialogue menu to ask \"Any rumors?\" and receive a dynamic tip.\n- Tutorialization: The Rumormonger now acts as an immersive guide, occasionally broadcasting tips to teach players about complex mechanics (e.g., Merchant synergies, Trash Man filters) naturally through gameplay.\n- Contextual Awareness: The Rumormonger actively parses and adapts to:\n  - Station Type: Dynamically identifies 12+ vanilla station scripts (Pre-cached in init.lua for performance).\n  - War Heat: Pulls live conflict data from the Cosmic War bridge.\n  - Faction Wealth: Differentiates between wealthy and poor economies.\n  - Geography: Certain rumors (like Deep Core lore) will not spawn near the Outer Rim.\n  - Player Reputation: Station inhabitants generally refuse to gossip with outlaws (cuts off at -30,000 rep), preventing hostile military outposts from offering out-of-character dialogue.\n  - Captain Synergy: Smuggler and Explorer captains know how to quietly buy drinks and extract information even in highly hostile ports (extends interaction threshold down to -60,000 reputation).\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a1', 'Captains Logs'%_t, 'Hooks directly into the Cosmic Overhaul background command simulation.\n\nKey Mechanics:\n\n- When a captain completes a map command (Scout, Mine, Trade, etc.) and sends the player a mail report, a narrative "Captain\'s Log" is dynamically appended to the bottom of the message.\n- Context Validation: Logs react directly to the parent faction and sector data where the operation took place. For example, trading in a high War Heat sector triggers logs detailing aggressive military patrols or close calls with blockades.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a2', 'Dynamic Narrative Events'%_t, 'A global event controller listens for hyperspace jumps and spawns immersive, world-building events based on the local geopolitical climate.\n\nAvailable Events:\n\n1. Refugee Convoys: (Triggers when War Heat > 40). Fleeing civilian ships appear with damaged hyperdrives. Players can donate Food or Medical Supplies to rescue them for reputation and rumors.\n   - Captain Synergy: Merchants negotiate Hazard Pay; Smugglers can skim supplies for massive credit payouts.\n2. Echoes of the Frontline (Graveyards): (Triggers when War Heat > 80). Players may stumble upon massive wreckage fields—the immediate aftermath of a fleet clash.\n3. Black Box Extraction: Players can interact with Stashes in Graveyards to extract audio logs, System Upgrades and credits.\n   - Captain Synergy: Scavengers and Explorers extract 25-50% more value and Exceptional upgrades.\n4. Cinematic Monuments: (Deep inside AI territory). Spawns colossal procedural monuments. Reading the inscription grants a permanent +1500 reputation boost.\n5. Drifting Ghost Ship: Intercept a faint distress signal from a derelict freighter and trigger a narrative dialog.\n6. Rogue AI Probe: Spawns a fast, evasive military probe that scales shields and damage up to 500% near the Core. Destroy it before it escapes with scanned data.\n7. Stranded Diplomat: A faction\'s diplomat is stranded in hostile space. Extract them before capture.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a3', 'Synergy Updates'%_t, '- Corrupted Lore Nodes: Data caches in Eclipse territory offer 2x rewards but instantly spawn a massive Ascendancy ambush.\n- Explorer Resonance: Ships commanded by an Explorer captain gain a +400% (range 250) interaction range on Black Boxes.\n- Galactic Lore Broadcasts: Finding a Legendary subsystem or massive credits in a data cache broadcasts your discovery globally via Cosmic Vault News.\n- Famine Relief Anomalies: Interact with emergency relief caches during severe faction famines to either steal the loot or donate it for massive reputation (+25,000) and instant famine reduction.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a4', 'Rift DLC Interoperability'%_t, '- Classified Rift Tech: Recovered Black Boxes now have a chance to drop highly-classified Rift Research Data and Subclass Subsystems. These contraband goods are extremely valuable on the black market.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a5', 'Cosmic Vault Synergy'%_t, '- Deep Economy Integration: Ambient Galactic News events (Trade Crisis & Market Boom) seamlessly tie into the CosmicVaultEconomy API, natively spiking or dropping a faction\'s active Famine Score.\n- Dead Empire Filter: Galactic News Generation natively utilizes FactionEradicationUtility to strictly filter out destroyed empires, preventing ghost factions from broadcasting messages.\n- Post-Boss Anomalies: Upon destroying the infamous Bottan Dreadnought, the game natively invokes CosmicVaultAnomalies to spawn a persistent SpatialRift anomaly for advanced exploration.\n- Unified News API: Legacy news broadcasting systems are securely passed through the new CosmicVaultNews architecture for global validation.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a6', 'Network Safety & Anti-Cheat'%_t, '- Math.Random Fix: Unstable Lua math.random calls are replaced with Avorion\'s deterministic random():getInt() sequence. This guarantees 100% synchronization on Multiplayer Dedicated Servers and prevents cascading desyncs.\n- Callable Validation: UI and background scripts have been fully hardened. Malicious clients can no longer spoof "free" remote calls; the server actively verifies execution contexts before processing any requests, sealing Arbitrary Code Execution (ACE) vulnerabilities.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a7', 'Vanilla Bug Fixes'%_t, '- Scout Mission Fix: We patched a massive, long-standing vanilla bug where Scout Missions would completely skip and ignore Faction Headquarters sectors because the native dialogue trees were missing the template definition.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a8', 'Galactic News & Economy'%_t, 'Cosmic Chronicles adds a living economy and news network to the galaxy.\n\nKey Features:\n\n- Galactic News Network: Real-time broadcasts of sector events like economic booms, pirate invasions, and trade blockades.\n- Stock Market: Invest in various galactic commodities and faction indices that fluctuate dynamically based on galaxy events.\n- Dynamic Local Events: Gold rushes, trade blockades, and shortages that physically alter sectors and trading profits.\n- Deep Space Discoveries: Find massive, bespoke monoliths, data caches, and lore fragments hidden in uncharted sectors.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a9', 'The Vanilla Way vs The Cosmic Way'%_t, 'Vanilla Avorion features "Radio Chatter", which randomly prints static strings over station models without any context.\n\nThe Cosmic Way: The Rumormonger system completely overrides this. Every piece of dialogue you see floating above a station, or spoken to you in the docking menu, is dynamically built. It considers the station type, the local economy, the faction\'s current war heat, and your specific captain\'s subclass before choosing what to say.\n'%_t, '')
end
